/E (DeFi has produced numerous "stablecoins" pegged to external assets like USD. These require external oracles: trusted third parties who attest to off-chain prices. This introduces trust assumptions and attack surfaces.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
149 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 70 0 R
/E (What if we could build a steadycoin using only on-chain data? Oracle contract would parse and verify headers and coinbases and emit BCHEH price information to other contracts. This is already feasible with BCH's current smart contract capabilities, though careful design is required to work around coinbase transaction sizes and possibility of forks and reorgs. Such oracle would have SPV \(simple payment verification\) security which would make the price information as secure as the accumulated blockchain proof-of-work.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
